From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:55:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Refuse a DP power-on in USB3-only mode

In USB3-only mode the Type-C partner has no DisplayPort lanes and the DP
PCS stays in reset, so a DP power-on cannot succeed. It still runs the
DP lane table and the DP TX tuning over the TX lane blocks, which on a
PHY without dedicated DP TX blocks are the lanes of the active USB3
link. After the following CX power collapse the USB3 link no longer
detects partners on that port.

Return -ENOLINK from qmp_combo_dp_power_on() in USB3-only mode without
touching the hardware.

Such a power-on comes from DRM re-enabling a DisplayPort output whose
sink has gone away, for example when the fbdev emulation restores its
mode at system suspend. Why DRM does that is a separate question; the
PHY must not reprogram the USB3 lanes for it either way.

A mode request that arrives while no user holds the PHY used to be
dropped by typec_mux_set(), since the preliminary USB4 support, so the
next initialisation could program a stale mode, such as USB3-only for a
DisplayPort sink, which this check would then refuse. Record that mode
for the next initialisation, as the driver did before.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index a1279ecf177..46615f21c54 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -4480,6 +4480,20 @@ static int qmp_combo_dp_power_on(struct phy *phy)
 
 	mutex_lock(&qmp->phy_mutex);
 
+	/*
+	 * In USB3-only mode the Type-C partner has no DisplayPort lanes and
+	 * the DP PCS stays in reset: a DP power-on can only fail, and its lane
+	 * writes would overwrite the TX configuration of the active USB3 lanes.
+	 * This happens when DRM re-enables a stale DP output (e.g. the fbdev
+	 * restore at system suspend) after the sink went away; after a CX
+	 * collapse the USB3 link then no longer detects partners.
+	 */
+	if (qmp->qmpphy_mode == QMPPHY_MODE_USB3_ONLY) {
+		dev_dbg(qmp->dev, "DP power-on refused in USB3-only mode\n");
+		ret = -ENOLINK;
+		goto out_unlock;
+	}
+
 	qmp_combo_dp_serdes_init(qmp);
 
 	qmp_combo_dp_lane_blocks(qmp, &use_tx, &use_tx2);
@@ -5403,9 +5417,15 @@ static int qmp_combo_typec_mux_set(struct typec_mux_dev *mux, struct typec_mux_s
 		return 0;
 	}
 
-	/* The mux still receives Type-C events, even if all PHYs are uninitialized */
-	if (!qmp->init_count)
+	/*
+	 * The mux still receives Type-C events, even if all PHYs are
+	 * uninitialized. Keep the mode for the next initialization, which
+	 * would otherwise program a stale one, e.g. USB3-only for a DP sink.
+	 */
+	if (!qmp->init_count) {
+		qmp->qmpphy_mode = new_mode;
 		return 0;
+	}
 
 	return qmp_combo_reconfigure_phy(qmp, new_mode);
 }
